ains a set of trivial fixes for all the C4701 warnings \\(just\ninitializing variables to 0 or NULL or appropriate error code\\) to make sure\nthat deterministic values will be returned from all the execution paths.\n\nRT#3835\n\nSigned-off-by: Matt Caswell <matt@openssl.org>\n\nMatt's note: All of these appear to be bogus warnings, i.e. there isn't\nactually a code path where an unitialised variable could be used - its just\nthat the compiler hasn't been able to figure that out from the logic. So\nthis commit is just about silencing spurious warnings.\n\nReviewed-by: Rich Salz <rsalz@openssl.org>\")\n\nShow description for 4c9b0a0 \n\nGunnar Kudrjavets \n\nauthored and \n\n[ mattcaswell ](/openssl/openssl/commits?author=mattcaswell)\n\ncommitted  on May 6, 2015 \n\n[ 4c9b0a0  ](/openssl/openssl/commit/4c9b0a0314c8bab3c9faeac06d0aa734836b2f81)\n\nCopy full SHA for 4c9b0a0 \n\n[ ](/openssl/openssl/blob/4c9b0a0314c8bab3c9faeac06d0aa734836b2f81/crypto/asn1/tasn_dec.c) [ ](/openssl/openssl/tree/4c9b0a0314c8bab3c9faeac06d0aa734836b2f81)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on May 1, 2015 \n\n  * ####  [ free null cleanup finale ](/openssl/openssl/commit/b548a1f11c06ccdfa4f52a539912d22d77ee309e \"free null cleanup finale\n\nDon't check for NULL before calling OPENSSL_free\n\nReviewed-by: Richard Levitte <levitte@openssl.org>\")\n\nShow description for b548a1f \n\nRich Salz \n\ncommitted  on May 1, 2015 \n\n[ b548a1f  ](/openssl/openssl/commit/b548a1f11c06ccdfa4f52a539912d22d77ee309e)\n\nCopy full SHA for b548a1f \n\n[ ](/openssl/openssl/blob/b548a1f11c06ccdfa4f52a539912d22d77ee309e/crypto/asn1/tasn_dec.c) [ ](/openssl/openssl/tree/b548a1f11c06ccdfa4f52a539912d22d77ee309e)\n\nMore actions \n\n\n\n\n<::before>\n\n###  Commits on Mar 28, 2015 \n\n  * ####  [ Make asn1_ex_i2c, asn1_ex_c2i static. ](/openssl/openssl/commit/23dc1706e8727642ee7bc3dc985a3068a524e3bd \"Make asn1_ex_i2c, asn1_ex_c2i static.\n\nReviewed-by: Kurt Roeckx <kurt@openssl.org>\")\n\nShow d